<p class="lede">Bayan 0.4.1 is the current release, a prerelease. It builds on 0.4.0, the release where the compiler became a Bayan program that needs only a C compiler. This page covers both. The full list is in the <a href="https://github.com/ikhbat-org/bayan/blob/v0.4.1/CHANGELOG.md">CHANGELOG</a>.</p>

<h2 id="self-hosted">A compiler written in Bayan</h2>
<p>The compiler, its test runner and the language server are Bayan programs. The repository keeps the compiler as one C file, <code>bootstrap/bayan.c</code>, so you can build it with any C11 compiler and nothing else. <a href="install.html#build">Install Bayan</a> has the command.</p>

<h2 id="lsp">The language server ships with the compiler</h2>
<p>Every release archive holds <code>bayan-lsp</code> (<code>bayan-lsp.exe</code> on Windows) beside <code>bayan</code>. Point your editor's language client at it; <a href="https://github.com/ikhbat-org/bayan/blob/v0.4.1/editors/README.md">editors/README.md</a> describes the VS Code extension.</p>

<h2 id="test">bayan test runs golden cases</h2>
<p><code>bayan test tests/cases</code> runs the compiler's golden cases itself, programs beside the output they must give, and prints one line per failing case with its first differing line.</p>

<h2 id="std">New in the standard library</h2>
<ul>
<li><code>std.regex</code>: <code>Regex.parse</code>, then <code>matches</code>, <code>find</code>, <code>findAll</code>, <code>replaced(text, by:)</code> and <code>Regex.escaped</code>. Matching takes time linear in the length of the text.</li>
<li><code>std.encoding</code>: <code>Base64.encode</code> and <code>Base64.decode</code>.</li>
<li>Glob patterns: <code>Glob.matches(pattern, for: path)</code> in <code>std.path</code>, and <code>glob(pattern)</code> in <code>std.fs</code>, which lists the files a pattern names.</li>
</ul>
