<h2 id="fixes">Fixes in 0.4.1</h2>
<p>0.4.1 closes holes where the compiler accepted unsafe programs: borrows kept across loop iterations, returned through <code>out</code> or read in <code>defer</code>; moves inside <code>defer</code>; an undeclared effect after a call to a function that declares <code>uses</code>; and interfaces whose methods differ in states or error sets. A branch that ends in <code>fail</code> now narrows the rest of the block as <code>return</code> does, and a raw string whose text shares the closing <code>"""</code> line keeps that text.</p>

<h2 id="limits">Known limits</h2>
<p>These are still open in 0.4.1:</p>
<ul>
<li>A mutable <code>Span</code> can write through a <code>let</code> binding.</li>
<li><code>requires</code> checks on fields miss <code>ref</code> and <code>out</code> arguments and nested fields.</li>
<li>The implicit conversion from a string to bytes, and compound assignment through <code>xs[i].f</code>, evaluate an operand twice.</li>
<li>A <code>#!</code> script's cache entry does not cover the modules it imports, so after you change only an imported module <code>bayan run</code> can start the old binary. <code>bayan clean --cache</code> empties the cache.</li>
<li>A <code>become</code> payload that borrows a parameter is not fully checked.</li>
</ul>
